                <pb facs="0254" n="174" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg174"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">From the Peking Gazette of August 5, 1902.</hi></head>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">edict.</hi></p>
                <p>Ts’en Ch’un-hsuan is hereby commanded to come to Peking for audience.</p>
                <p>Ting Chen-toh not having as yet reached his post as governor of Shan-si, we
                    command Chao Erh-hsun to be governor of that province for the time being.</p>
                <p>Respect this.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
